{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneRTSurgeryConstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneRTSurgeryConstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BWVacuumRowIsHecke","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.rtData_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.rtData_two","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRTSurgeryConstruction.lean#L120-L131","doc":"**Non-vacuity model — the `n = 2` modular category over `ℚ`.** Two labels, both quantum\ndimension `1`, `D = 2` (`D ≠ 0`), one-component surgery with `colInv ≡ 1`. Confirms `RTSurgeryData`\nis inhabited, so `partitionSum`, `partitionSum_eq_dD`, and the `bwS0` discharge are not vacuous. Its\n`partitionSum = Σ_λ (1/2)·1 = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.bwS0_eq_smul_of_rt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.bwS0_eq_smul_of_rt","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRTSurgeryConstruction.lean#L107-L114","doc":"Corollary: under the RT identification, `bwS0` is a *nonzero rescaling of the quantum-dimension\nvector*, `bwS0 λ = (1/D)·d_λ` — no per-block freedom. This is the exact content the four failed\ngeometric-realisation routes were trying to reproduce independently; the RT construction supplies it\nstructurally (modulo the two named inputs). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.bwS0_eq_dD_of_rt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.bwS0_eq_dD_of_rt","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRTSurgeryConstruction.lean#L91-L105","doc":"**The RT discharge of `bwS0_eq_hecke`, conditional on the two named irreducible inputs.**\n\nLet `bwS0 : ι → R` be the abstract Chern–Simons gauge vacuum row. Given\n\n* `(RT)` `hrt : ∀ λ, bwS0 λ = S_{0λ}` — the gauge datum **is** the RT surgery per-label weight\n  (the cited WRT = CS partition-function / Kirby-invariance theorem), and\n* the reading of `M.d`, `M.D` as the **Hecke** modular data `(BW = Hecke)`,\n\nthen `bwS0 λ = d_λ/D`. The proof is the one-line composition with the proved `S0`; **all** of the\nopen content sits in the two hypotheses, correctly attributed (one cited pure-math theorem, one\nphysics identification). This is `bwse` stated precisely — not closed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.vacuum_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.vacuum_weight","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRTSurgeryConstruction.lean#L86-L89","doc":"The vacuum label enters with weight `S_{00} = 1/D` (its quantum dimension is `1`) — the RT\ninvariant of the empty surgery (`S³`) is `S_{00} = 1/D`, the standard normalisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.surgeryWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.surgeryWeight","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRTSurgeryConstruction.lean#L83-L84","doc":"The RT weight of a single label `λ` is exactly `S_{0λ} = d_λ/D`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.partitionSum_eq_dD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.partitionSum_eq_dD","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRTSurgeryConstruction.lean#L74-L81","doc":"**The RT per-label weight is the modular S-matrix vacuum row `d_λ/D`.** Rewriting the assembly\nwith the proved `S0` definition exhibits each label `λ` entering the RT invariant with weight\n`d_λ/D` — the sole appearance of the vacuum row in the manifold invariant, and the object `bwS0`\nmust equal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.partitionSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.partitionSum","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRTSurgeryConstruction.lean#L66-L72","doc":"**The Reshetikhin–Turaev surgery invariant** of the presented 3-manifold: the color-sum of the\nframed colored-link invariant weighted by the S-matrix vacuum row `S_{0λ}`. This is the shape of\nTuraev's surgery formula `τ(M) = Σ_λ S_{0λ} · F(L, λ)` (global framing normaliser dropped). The\nsum is over the modular category's simple objects; the **per-label weight is the vacuum row**.\n\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] Reshetikhin–Turaev surgery formula (Turaev 1994, ch. II). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.colInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.colInv","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRTSurgeryConstruction.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The framed colored-link invariant `F(L, λ)` of the surgery link colored by `λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.labels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.labels","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRTSurgeryConstruction.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The fusion labels summed over in the surgery presentation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRTSurgeryConstruction.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.toVerlindeVacuumRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData.toVerlindeVacuumRow","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRTSurgeryConstruction.lean#L56-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RTSurgery.RTSurgeryData","kind":"structure","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRTSurgeryConstruction.lean#L51-L60","doc":"**RT surgery data.** The modular S-matrix vacuum row (`VerlindeVacuumRow`), together with the\ndata of a surgery presentation of the 3-manifold: the finite set of fusion `labels`, and the framed\n**colored-link invariant** `colInv λ = F(L, λ)` — the value of the RT ribbon functor on the surgery\nlink `L` with its component colored by `λ`. (The framing/signature normaliser is a global scalar\nthat cancels in every per-label / ratio statement below, so it is not carried.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}